{"audio": "2timothy-04.opus", "voice": "Davis", "duration_ms": 142267, "sentences": [{"start_ms": 0, "end_ms": 1867, "text": "2 Timothy, Chapter Four."}, {"start_ms": 1867, "end_ms": 16133, "text": "I charge thee therefore before God, and the Lord Jesus Christ, who shall judge the quick and the dead at his appearing and his kingdom; Preach the word; be instant in season, out of season; reprove, rebuke, exhort with all longsuffering and doctrine."}, {"start_ms": 16133, "end_ms": 28400, "text": "For the time will come when they will not endure sound doctrine; but after their own lusts shall they heap to themselves teachers, having itching ears; And they shall turn away their ears from the truth, and shall be turned unto fables."}, {"start_ms": 28400, "end_ms": 36267, "text": "But watch thou in all things, endure afflictions, do the work of an evangelist, make full proof of thy ministry."}, {"start_ms": 36267, "end_ms": 40667, "text": "For I am now ready to be offered, and the time of my departure is at hand."}, {"start_ms": 40667, "end_ms": 53733, "text": "I have fought a good fight, I have finished my course, I have kept the faith: Henceforth there is laid up for me a crown of righteousness, which the Lord, the righteous judge, shall give me at that day: and not to me only, but unto all them also that love his appearing."}, {"start_ms": 53733, "end_ms": 65467, "text": "Do thy diligence to come shortly unto me: For Demas hath forsaken me, having loved this present world, and is departed unto Thessalonica; Crescens to Galatia, Titus unto Dalmatia."}, {"start_ms": 65467, "end_ms": 67067, "text": "Only Luke is with me."}, {"start_ms": 67067, "end_ms": 71600, "text": "Take Mark, and bring him with thee: for he is profitable to me for the ministry."}, {"start_ms": 71600, "end_ms": 73600, "text": "And Tychicus have I sent to Ephesus."}, {"start_ms": 73600, "end_ms": 80933, "text": "The cloke that I left at Troas with Carpus, when thou comest, bring with thee, and the books, but especially the parchments."}, {"start_ms": 80933, "end_ms": 90533, "text": "Alexander the coppersmith did me much evil: the Lord reward him according to his works: Of whom be thou ware also; for he hath greatly withstood our words."}, {"start_ms": 90533, "end_ms": 98533, "text": "At my first answer no man stood with me, but all men forsook me: I pray God that it may not be laid to their charge."}, {"start_ms": 98533, "end_ms": 110533, "text": "Notwithstanding the Lord stood with me, and strengthened me; that by me the preaching might be fully known, and that all the Gentiles might hear: and I was delivered out of the mouth of the lion."}, {"start_ms": 110533, "end_ms": 119200, "text": "And the Lord shall deliver me from every evil work, and will preserve me unto his heavenly kingdom: to whom be glory for ever and ever."}, {"start_ms": 119200, "end_ms": 120000, "text": "Amen."}, {"start_ms": 120000, "end_ms": 123867, "text": "Salute Prisca and Aquila, and the household of Onesiphorus."}, {"start_ms": 123867, "end_ms": 129467, "text": "Erastus abode at Corinth: but Trophimus have I left at Miletum sick."}, {"start_ms": 129467, "end_ms": 132400, "text": "Do thy diligence to come before winter."}, {"start_ms": 132400, "end_ms": 137467, "text": "Eubulus greeteth thee, and Pudens, and Linus, and Claudia, and all the brethren."}, {"start_ms": 137467, "end_ms": 140267, "text": "The Lord Jesus Christ be with thy spirit."}, {"start_ms": 140267, "end_ms": 141467, "text": "Grace be with you."}, {"start_ms": 141467, "end_ms": 142267, "text": "Amen."}], "words": [{"t": "2", "s": 0, "e": 422, "si": 0}, {"t": "Timothy,", "s": 422, "e": 783, "si": 0}, {"t": "Chapter", "s": 1104, "e": 1425, "si": 0}, {"t": "Four.", "s": 1586, "e": 1767, "si": 0}, {"t": "I", "s": 2287, "e": 2307, "si": 1}, {"t": "charge", "s": 2387, "e": 2747, "si": 1}, {"t": "thee", "s": 2807, "e": 2947, "si": 1}, {"t": "therefore", "s": 2967, "e": 3408, "si": 1}, {"t": "before", "s": 3428, "e": 3768, "si": 1}, 